{
  "_comment": [
    "District vocabulary, per state, authored FROM the three source bulletins.",
    "Karnataka and Rajasthan spell their districts in Latin; Uttar Pradesh spells",
    "",
    "Rajasthan carries all 41 districts as of the December 2024 reorganisation (the original 33 plus the 8 retained new ones), not only those named in the bundled bulletin -- a district the vocabulary does not know cannot be published as coverage even when the bulletin advises on it.",
    "them in Devanagari. The 'aliases' lists carry spelling variants AND the",
    "glyph-corrupted forms these specific PDFs actually emit (e.g. the UP file",
    "renders 'shaahjahaanpur' with a mis-mapped consonant). Absorbing the",
    "corruption here is what makes rules-first resolution work on real files.",
    "",
    "areaCode scheme is OPENAGRI-DISTRICT, not LGD. LGD is the correct national",
    "scheme for an Indian district but its codes are numeric and we do not have",
    "the master loaded; emitting a readable code we can vouch for beats emitting",
    "a number we cannot. See README 'Known limits'."
  ],
